  "title": "Rotational shallow water equations with viscous damping and boundary control: structure-preserving spatial discretization",
  "abstract": "© The Author(s), under exclusive licence to Springer-Verlag London Ltd., part of Springer Nature 2024.This paper is dedicated to structure-preserving spatial discretization of shallow water dynamics. First, a port-Hamiltonian formulation is provided for the two-dimensional rotational shallow water equations with viscous damping. Both tangential and normal boundary port variables are introduced. Then, the corresponding weak form is derived and a partitioned finite element method is applied to obtain a finite-dimensional continuous-time port-Hamiltonian approximation. Four simulation scenarios are investigated to illustrate the approach and show its effectiveness.",
  "authkeywords": [
    "Partitioned finite element method (PFEM)",
    "Port-Hamiltonian systems (pHs)",
    "Shallow water equations (SWE)",
    "Viscous damping"
